<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bechara El Khoury</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1890–1964</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Bishara al-Khuri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bechara El Khoury was a Maronite lawyer and politician who became the first president of independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a>, serving from 1943 to 1952. With the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riad-al-solh">Riad Al Solh</a> he agreed the unwritten <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-pact">National Pact</a> of 1943, which shared the main offices of state among religious communities. His arrest by the French in November 1943 provoked the protests that won independence; corruption charges forced his resignation in 1952.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bechara-el-khoury.jpg" alt="Bechara El Khoury" width="320" height="485" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bechara_El_Khoury_-_1947.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
